# - 24Hip-Hop, Eye Spy finds its groove at the intersection of Bouyon and culture (opened 2026-10-20): Eye Spy released January 16, 2026, first collaboration between Klassik Frescobar and V'GHN, grounded in Bouyon rhythmic backbone, produced by DJ Kalli and Boogy Rankss, sample from the anime Inuyasha, concept mapped in a short session after connecting with the producers in New York, V'GHN part completed within a day; Klassik Frescobar born Kamaal Burrowes, originally from Jamaica, now based in Miami; Dansa earned a nomination for Best Soca & Dennery Song of the Year at the Caribbean Music Awards.
# - Deezer, Klassik Frescobar artist page (opened 2026-10-20): Jamaican-American singer of Caribbean music specialising in soca; musical influence began in the early 1990s in his hometown of Kingston, Jamaica, Constant Spring Gardens neighbourhood, listening to Bounty Killa, the owner Paul and Beenie Man on his mother cassette recorder; emigrated to the Bronx, made rap while staying close to dancehall parties, relationships with DJs and producers including Ricky Blaze; moved to Miami in 2014, worked closely with Red Cafe; made his name on the Miami soca scene with Boom, Bee Sting and Chair in 2019; viral Looking Good (Code Red Riddim) in 2020, #LookingGoodChallenge over three million views; singles Like Dat Remix with GBM Nutron (2021), Too Much with Marzville (2021), Eye Watch (2022), Make Contact (2022), Pose (2023), Bigman (2023), Instruction Time (2024), Choppa Slide (2024); Bronxghanistan EP in 2024 with seven tracks; in 2025 Sal Gason and the hit Dansa, which reached No. 21 in the overseas charts. Deezer biography repeatedly prints the variant Klassik Escobar.
# - Shazam, Dansa song page (opened 2026-10-20): published January 24, 2025; written by Kallicharran Randy Changoo, Kamaal Burrowes and Norris E. Hamilton.
# - Shazam, Boom (Fuego Riddim) song page (opened 2026-10-20): released August 1, 2019 by Island Circle, 109 BPM; writers Kamaal Burrowes, Lashley Winter, Kevin Alexander and Anwar Dacosta.
# - Shazam, Forever song page (opened 2026-10-20): released December 27, 2024 as part of the album Bronxghanistan, label Klassik Frescobar, writer Kamaal Burrowes.
# - Shazam, V'ghn artist page (opened 2026-10-20): lists Eye Spy, Single, credited DJ Kalli, Klassik Frescobar & V'ghn, among his 2026 releases.
# - The Source, Klassik Frescobar brings Soca to the world with Dansa (opened 2026-10-20, published 2026-06-17): SocaRecords ranked Dansa the second most important soca song of 2025; Caribbean Music Award nominations for Soca Song of the Year and Dennery Song of the Year; first soca track to enter Spotify Viral 100 chart in France in a decade, No. 2 Viral in Nigeria, No. 1 in Sierra Leone, iTunes number ones from Uganda to Switzerland; nearly 15 million Spotify streams; included in Spotify UK Carnival Sounds campaign and Notting Hill Carnival promotion; based in Miami; earlier attention through Boom, Looking Good and Too Much; visualizer filmed in front of a Florida liquor store; TikTok driven rise.
# - SocaRecords, Soca Year-End Top 25 and Dansa audience analysis (search results, 2026-10-20): Dansa finishes 2025 as the No. 2 soca song of the year, produced by DJ Kalli & Boogy Rankss, released late January 2025, close to 10 million Spotify streams at year end, growth driven largely by African markets, notably Kenya and Nigeria; iTunes World No. 1 in France, Australia, the United Kingdom, Uganda, Denmark, Switzerland, Grenada, Mauritius, Thailand, Canada, Trinidad & Tobago, Antigua & Barbuda, the Netherlands and the Bahamas, No. 3 in the United States.
# - Jamz Podcast, Soca/Bouyon 2025-26 mix tracklist (search result, 2026-10-20): Reno x Klassik Frescobar, Perfect, listed in a soca and bouyon mix. No platform song page for Perfect was opened in this research, so Perfect is discussed as mixtape circulation only and is NOT in the schema track list.
# - Older biographical portraits (search results, 2026-10-20): Film Daily, Muzique Magazine, HipHopSince1987 and The Source 2021 profile agree that he was born in New York, raised in Kingston, Jamaica by his grandparents, returned to New York at 13; a She Got Game Media portrait recounts the early stage name Sikk, later Klassik, with Frescobar built from fresh and bar. These accounts conflict with the shorter originally from Jamaica formulation, and the profile presents the conflict instead of hiding it.
# Note: Klassik Frescobar is a soca and Dennery Segment artist, not a Dominican bouyon artist. He is on this site through verified bouyon contact points only: Eye Spy, the Boogy Rankss production hinge, Take Dat with Trixzmigos as documented in the wave 17 research, and Perfect in bouyon mixes.

